course: dictionary
lesson: 10650
title: Units
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A unit is a name for a measure or a single part. In maths, units tell you what you are measuring or counting: a meter, a kilogram, a liter or an hour. Always write the unit with your answer, because 5 on its own does not say 5 of what.
explain: «The biggest pack is often cheaper per unit, but not always, so always do the sum.» Per unit means for each one. To find out which pack is the better buy, work out the price of one unit for each pack, then compare them. Do the sum, then decide.
explain: Units also show place value. In 47, the 7 is in the units place, which means the ones. A unit can also be a part of a course: Unit 3 might be about fractions. The words around the word tell you which meaning is being used.
fact: A unit is an amount used for measuring, like a meter, a kilogram, a liter or an hour.
fact: A unit is a single thing, person or group that is part of something bigger.
fact: The units place is the place for single numbers: in 47, the 7 is in the units place.
fact: «Price per unit» means the cost of one single item.
fact: In «Mice use pipes, cables and gaps behind kitchen units», a kitchen unit is a piece of furniture.
exercise: Which digit is in the units place of 47? | 470 | 40 | *7 | 4
exercise: Which of these is a unit of length? | *meter | liter | second | kilogram
exercise: «Mice use pipes, cables and gaps behind kitchen units.» In this sentence, what is a kitchen unit? | A type of mouse | *A piece of furniture | A kitchen light | A kind of food
test: In «Unit 3 is about fractions», what does unit mean? | A kind of fraction | A single number on a ruler | A measuring cup | *A part of a course
test: Which number has 9 in the units place? | *19 | 9 | 190 | 91
exam: Sam buys 4 cartons, and each carton holds 1 liter. What is the total, with its unit? | 4 | *4 liters | 1 liter | 5 liters
